sub:assertion {
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/darwin1859-ch12-15> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/Claim>;
    dc:description "The inhabitants of any area (oceanic islands, mountains, lakes, marshes, caves), where not identical, are plainly related to those of the region from which colonists could most readily have come, the colonists having since been modified and better fitted to their new homes.";
    dc:type "historical-inference";
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Inhabitants of any area are modified colonists from the most accessible source";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/context> "Charles Darwin, On the Origin of Species (1st ed., London: John Murray, 1859), Chapter XII, “Geographical Distribution, continued”; section “On colonisation from the nearest source with subsequent modification”. Scope: biotas of islands, mountains, lakes, marshes and caves"
}
